cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. In academic work, please also cite the companion Scientific Reports paper once its full reference is added here."
title: "RAIR-Sim: a compartmental simulator of radioactive iodine therapy response in metastatic thyroid cancer"
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: "Marie"
    family-names: "Fusella Giuntini"
  - given-names: "Cyril"
    family-names: "Voyant"
    affiliation: "Mines Paris - PSL, O.I.E. Laboratory, France"
    website: "https://person.cyrilvoyant.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0242-7377"

repository-code: "https://github.com/MarieFG49/CTD_SIMU_RAI"
license: "MIT"
version: "1.0.0"

abstract: >
  A compartmental (ODE-based) simulator of the therapeutic response to
  radioactive iodine (RAI) therapy in metastatic thyroid cancer. Three
  coupled ordinary differential equations (administered activity, tumor
  cell number, thyroglobulin biomarker) are solved in closed form fraction
  by fraction, letting clinicians explore how the number of iratherapy
  sessions, the interval between sessions, and the administered activity
  affect the simulated biomarker trajectory, for both RAI-responding and
  RAI-refractory virtual patients. Includes an interactive MATLAB App
  Designer interface (RAIR-Sim) and scripted sensitivity-analysis tools.

keywords:
  - radioactive iodine therapy
  - thyroid cancer
  - digital twin
  - pharmacodynamic modeling
  - compartmental model
  - thyroglobulin
  - treatment optimization
  - MATLAB

